{
 "translation": "Thus, when Sundarlal Babu, along with his companions Rasalu and Nekiram etc., would sing \"Hath Laiyan Kumhlanani Lajwanti De Boote\" while taking out the morning procession, Sundarlal's voice would immediately stop, and he would walk silently, thinking about Lajwanti: \"Where would she be? In what condition would she be? What would she be thinking about us? Will she ever come back or not?\" And walking on the stony floor, his steps would falter. And now it had come to such a pass that he had stopped thinking about Lajwanti altogether. His sorrow had now become the sorrow of the world. He had to escape his own pain.",
